With index notation and the contraction $epsilon_(i j k) epsilon_(p q k) = delta_(i p) delta_(j q) - delta_(i q) delta_(j p)$, the $i$th component of the left-hand side is
$ (vb(a) times (vb(b) times vb(c)))_i & = epsilon_(i j k) a_j epsilon_(k p q) b_p c_q \
                    & = (delta_(i p) delta_(j q) - delta_(i q) delta_(j p)) a_j b_p c_q \
                    & = (vb(a) dot vb(c)) b_i - (vb(a) dot vb(b)) c_i, $
which is precisely the $i$th component of the right-hand side.
